  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi></math>&nbsp;be the set of all&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;for which the system of linear equations</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p>has no solution. Then the set&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi></math></p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Contains more than two elements",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Is an empty set",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Is a singleton",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Contains exactly two elements",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>&nbsp;For no&nbsp;solution <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> and at least one of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#916;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>&#916;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>&#916;</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> is non-zero.<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mi>&#955;</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mi>&#955;</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#916;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mi>&#955;</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>4</mn></mtd><mtd><mi>&#955;</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>&nbsp;And for&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mo>&#8710;</mo><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br />Hence, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p>"
  }
